{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T065458Z_dev-02_staged_1931", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray analysis sets its one-sided 95% upper limit where 2Δln L = 2.71 (TS drop of 2.71), profiling over the dwarfs' J-factors (a Gaussian prior on log10 of a per-dwarf J normalization, range [-3,3]). The AMS-02 antiproton analysis instead uses ΔQ = Δ(-2lnL) = 3.84, the two-sided/nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold, and takes the upper endpoint. The paper notes this differs from the usual one-sided 2.71. It profiles over the diffusive-halo half-height L, with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197) and range 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 10.875, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19594, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1222, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11268, "cache_read_input_tokens": 15360, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T06:55:09+00:00"}
